# implements-port slice 11 (B2; Q43): unit_s7_prim_cross over its own convert.lm2 whose size_t -> int row has a
# Structure for its receiver (tests/unit_s7_conv_cellneed_table.lm2).  The table is read (a Structure is one
# cell); the conversion this program needs takes that row, and its receiver cell gives no name: said at the
# cell, "a conversion table cell this row needs is not a name (evaluating a table argument is not ported yet)"
# -- not read as a default, not a refusal of the table.
fn: go () int
    int: a 1
    size_t: b 2U
    a: b
    return: a

int: k
k: go()
if: k = 2
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 1; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
